e years  uh while i'm a speaker barack obama was  president and harry reid was  majority leader for most of that time so  there is a way to handle the spending  issue  uh but at some point you're going to pay  the paper you can't run your household  uh when you keep spending more than what  you bring in you can't run a business  that way  and your government can't run that way  either  yeah i'm curious mr speaker you write in  the book uh this page 61  i don't think ronald reagan would  recognize the republican party today and  he sure as hell couldn't get elected in  it  as a matter of fact reagan would be the  most left-wing candidate in the gop  these days by a mile how do you describe  a trump voter clearly in 2016 he  expanded the base for republicans  white workers uh men and women so  so how saying that how do you explain  the trump phenomena over  2016 and 2020 trump somebody you voted  for  in 2020 ronald reagan raised taxes  ronald reagan was not uh was actually  pro-abortion  uh if he looked through reagan's record  uh he was the most pragmatic republican  uh that uh that we've ever elected uh  but he was a great communicator  and frankly he's the reason i became a  republican i'm far more conservative  than he is  or than he was uh but uh what what  donald trump did uh was to take a lot of  disaffected voters  some republicans some independents and  frankly a lot of democrats  uh disaffected by uh the eight years of  barack obama  uh the poor economic recovery what we  saw after  uh 2008 and uh he appealed to them  and brought them into the party and  frankly kept them even  most of them in 2020  but you're pretty critical of him in  this book i mean you're not you're  unvarnished in your criticism of him  listen donald trump will die nominee  if john donald trump needs 2024 would  you support him mr speaker  uh listen i don't do hypotheticals that  doesn't do anybody any good uh but  donald trump and i've been friends for a  long time  i supported him i